{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg72pCeXoNC1eZ9k8wNeL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the basic flow:\n\n**1. Install uv** (if you haven't)\n```bash\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\n# or: pip install uv / brew install uv\n```\n\n**2. Create the project**\n```bash\nuv init myproject      # new directory\ncd myproject\n```\nOr, to initialize in the current directory:\n```bash\nuv init\n```\n\nThis creates `pyproject.toml`, `main.py`, `README.md`, `.python-version`, and a git repo.\n\n**3. Add dependencies**\n```bash\nuv add requests\nuv add --dev pytest     # dev-only dependency\n```\nThe first `uv add` creates a `.venv` and a `uv.lock` lockfile automatically.\n\n**4. Run code**\n```bash\nuv run main.py\nuv run pytest\n```\n`uv run` keeps the environment in sync, so you don't need to activate the venv.\n\n**Useful options**\n- `uv init --lib myproject`: library layout (`src/` package)\n- `uv init --package myproject`: packaged app with a CLI entry point\n- `uv init --python 3.12`: pin the Python version\n- `uv python install 3.13`: have uv download a Python version\n- `uv sync`: install everything from the lockfile (e.g. after cloning)\n- `uv remove <pkg>`: remove a dependency\n\nCommit `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, and `.python-version`. Leave `.venv` out of version control. `uv init` already adds it to `.gitignore`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6754,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6754},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"185f2ddb-db13-4897-8459-edc09b1892d5","uuid":"f7af9ae3-0172-41f0-8591-566cf1985b5b","timestamp":"2026-1